														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-718673">
									

<p>yeah i'm not really trying for an "oh god oh god what do we do" panic sort of thing here but honestly if you could find out about something happening in advance that had the potential to destroy the world (or worse) and make plans accordingly, then you should make those plans a part of the security protocols regarding it.</p>
<p>and yes, we do need more classes of "end of the world" events. XK seems to be specifically for religious related end of the world scenarios, but we dont see much discussion of other potential end of the world scenarios, not sure why.</p>
<p>really in the end this SCP is actually "safe" until and unless SCP-225-2 ends up moving close to the earth's surface. at that point even if it doesnt come into contact with 225-1 it has great potential for destruction as the earth rotates stuff directly into it at high speeds. really the odds of the two coming into contact are low even in that scenario….it's just that if they did, then it DOES become "oh god"</p>
<p>then again for all we know they'd bounce off each other or pass right through. no way to tell! but it's the not knowing that makes it a big deal</p>

