			<div class="content" id="post-content-719750">
									

<p>Several issues:<br />
1. It's not Keter unless and until it demonstrates that it is a current existential threat to humanity. As long as it only might possibly become a threat, it's Euclid.<br />
2. Trying to keep thingies contained is not the only reason for posting guards. They're also there to keep nosy people out, so 225-1 needs guards even though it's not going anywhere.<br />
3. The biggest issue, though, and what ultimately earned my downvote, is the very visible nature of 225-2. Anyone and anything from government space agencies to backyard amateur astronomers could potentially discover 225-2, particularly when it burns through the <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Earth%27s_atmosphere#Structure_of_the_atmosphere">lower atmosphere</a>…. The Foundation's good at information suppression, but it ain't that good. Not sure how to fix it without making it invisible, but then it would become Mackenzie's <a href="/scp-245">LEO Object</a>.<br />
4. Beyond all that, upvoting your own article is considered bad form.</p>
<p>That said, I like the basic concept exploring irresistible force vs. immovable object. Just not like it is now.</p>

